      "text": "Technology can step in to help. It can fill the gaps to enhance and assist with daily life. Older adults are increasingly adopting smart devices with AI technology. A growing number of older adults have smartphones. In the US, 76% of those 65 and older are on a smartphone. And globally, smartphone adoption varies depending on a region's economy. For some time now, AI has been the backbone behind many of the devices used daily. For aging, AI technology is a critical component of tech devices that can reduce isolation by connecting older adults to family and friends that can help them stay informed about whether updates and community information. Tech can help improve health and wellness with wearable devices.",
